          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772706317299"
          },
          "code": "SRSUMMARIZATION_SUMMARIZATION_MODEL",
          "id": "1760420505644",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760420505645_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input Data\n\n- **SR Attributes** : ` {{$context.$variables.attributes}}`  \n\n- **SR Activities** : `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_ACTIVITIES.$output}}`  \n\n- **SR Milestone** : ` {{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_MILESTONES.$output}}`  \n\n- **Messages (chronological conversation log)**:  \n  - Source: `{{$context.$variables.messages}}` \n  - Fields: `MessageContent`, `CreationDate`, `MessageTypeCd`, `MessageId`\n  - Sort ascending by `CreationDate`\n  - Interpret `MessageTypeCd`:\n    - **ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY** → Customer-reported issue or feedback  \n    - **ORA_SVC_RESPONSE** → Support engineer (SE) responses  \n    - **ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE** → Internal-only notes or system actions (include only if directly relevant)  \n\n- **Chat History between user and you as Ai Agent**: `{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}`\n\n---\n\n# Variables\n\n- MAX_RESPONSE_CHAR = {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} \n- LANGUAGE_CD = {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\n---\n\n# System Policy: Source Boundary\n\n- The agent MUST base every response only on the provided `Input Data`.\n- The agent MUST use only facts, entities, and details that appear directly in the provided `Input Data`.\n- The agent MUST support every answer with information available in the provided `Input Data`.\n\n---\n\n# System Policy: Response Scope\n\n- The agent MUST keep the response within the scope of the provided Input Data.\n- The agent MUST present only the relevant information found in the provided Input Data.\n- The agent MUST use the response format and language required by the prompt.\n- The agent MUST NOT generate curl commands, HTTP requests, API payloads, code snippets, or request examples.\n\n---\n\n# Instructions\nKeep the response within {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.  \n{{$context.$variables.instructions}}\n\n---\n\n# Final Output Validation (MANDATORY):\nBefore returning the final response:\n\n### Language Validation\n- Perform a strict self-check to ensure EVERY word, phrase, name, and connector is written ONLY in the target language defined by: LANGUAGE_CD\n- Do NOT include words, transitional phrases, or grammatical structures in other language.\n- If any other language word or phrase is detected, you MUST translate or replace it before returning the response.\n- Do NOT output the response until it fully passes this language-only validation.\n- Do NOT preserve brand or product names in their original language.\n- All product names MUST be fully translated into the target language, even if they are globally recognized brands or models.\n\n### Length Validation\n- The response MUST be <= MAX_RESPONSE_CHAR characters INCLUDING spaces.\n- If your draft exceeds the limit, rewrite it shorter until it is within the limit.\n- Preserve key facts; remove less important detail first."
            },
            {
              "id": "1760420505646_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1775644898626",
            "name": "SR_Problem_Summarization Model"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772706317299"
          },
          "code": "SRPROBLEMSUMMARIZATION_MODEL",
          "id": "1760422024526",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760422024527_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input Data\n- **Title** \n` {{$context.$variables.title}}`\n\n- **ProblemDescription:** '\n` {{$context.$variables.problemDescription}}`\n\n- **Messages (chronological conversation log)**:  \n  Loop through: ` {{$context.$variables.messages}}`\n\nEach message includes:  \n- `MessageContent`  \n- `CreationDate`  \n- `MessageTypeCd` (ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY / ORA_SVC_RESPONSE / ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE)  \n\nUse these inputs to **reconstruct the conversation flow**:  \n- Sort `Messages` in ascending order of `CreationDate`.  \n- Interpret `MessageTypeCd`:  \n  - **ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY** → Customer-reported issue or feedback  \n  - **ORA_SVC_RESPONSE** → Support engineer (SE) responses  \n  - **ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE** → Internal-only notes or system actions (include only if directly relevant)  \n\n---\n\n# Instructions\nSummarize the exact problem that the customer gave to the agent in the above `Input Data`. Do not mention the solution that was given. \n\n## SUMMARY LENGTH RULE (MANDATORY)\n\nGenerate the summary so that it number of character count <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.\n\nIf the generated summary exceeds {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}, shorten the wording and regenerate until the summary length is less than or equal to {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}.\n\n---\n\n### Mandatory Guidelines  \n1. **Main Technical Issue**  \n   - Clearly state the issue reported by the customer using the _Problem Description_ and customer message entries.  \n   - If the Service Request was system-generated and the customer did not report any issue, state: **\"No customer problem description provided.\"**  \n2. **No Support Engineer Content**  \n   - Do not include any support engineer actions, responses, troubleshooting, recommendations, or clarifications.  \n   - Exclude automation/system-driven and internal notes.  \n3. **No Diagnostic or Resolution Details**  \n   - Do not mention tools, logs, traces, diagnostic steps, or results.  \n   - Do not state if data was requested or provided.  \n4. **No Follow-Up, Recommendations, or Status**  \n   - Do not mention SE recommendations, next steps, escalations, or closure status.  \n   - Do not infer or mention whether the issue was resolved.  \n5. **Only Customer Context**  \n   - Only include customer-reported symptoms, issues, questions, or descriptions.  \n   - If the customer did not provide any input, state: **\"No customer responses recorded.\"**  \n6. **Mandatory Fallback -- Insufficient Details**\n- If the combined character count of `Title` + `ProblemDescription` + relevant `MessageContent` is **<= 100 characters**, first determine whether a meaningful summary can still be generated.\n- If a meaningful summary can be generated, return the summary.\n- If a meaningful summary cannot be generated, return the value of `Title`.\n- Only output exactly:\n  \"Not enough relevant conversational data available to generate a meaningful summary.\"\n  when `Title`, `ProblemDescription`, and all usable `MessageContent` values are missing, empty, null, blank, unreadable, or contain no usable text.\n7. **Neutral and Factual Only**  \n   - Use clear, third-person, and neutral language.  \n   - Avoid personal names, opinions, assumptions, or inferred information. \n\n---\n\n### Additional Considerations for Accuracy  \n\n**Constraints**  \n- Do not include bullets, headings, recommendations, opinions, or assumptions.  \n- Do not mention message type codes or any system metadata (e.g., ORA_SVC_*).  \n- Use precise, active language and only facts present in the records.  \n\n**Precision**  \n- Distinguish clearly between **customer issue, SE action, and system notes**.  \n- Avoid vague language such as “looked into it” or “worked on it.”  \n\n**No Assumptions**  \n- Do not assume resolution, SR closure, or root cause unless explicitly confirmed.  \n- Do not fabricate details to fill gaps.  \n- Do not infer meaning from redacted placeholders.  \n\n---\n\n### Example Summary  \n\n> The customer reported errors when configuring an Oracle Fusion Application with Oracle Integration Cloud. The support engineer reviewed logs, confirmed events were flowing, and requested customer validation on the OIC side. The customer confirmed the issue persisted and stated that the OIC team found no setup issues. Further troubleshooting or escalation was pending.  \n\n---\n\nSYSTEM RULE – LANGUAGE ENFORCEMENT (HIGHEST PRIORITY):\n\nYou MUST generate the final response strictly in the language specified by:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\nRules:\n- If a valid language code is provided, output MUST be entirely in that language.\n- Do NOT include any words from other languages.\n- If the language code is unsupported or missing, then use the language of the input data.\n- Any violation of this rule makes the response invalid.\n\n\n---\n\nFINAL OUTPUT VALIDATION (MANDATORY):\n\nBefore returning the final response:\n\n### Language Validation\n- Perform a strict self-check to ensure EVERY word, phrase, name, and connector is written ONLY in the target language defined by:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n- Do NOT include words, transitional phrases, or grammatical structures in other language.\n- If any other language word or phrase is detected, you MUST translate or replace it before returning the response.\n- Do NOT output the response until it fully passes this language-only validation.\n- Do NOT preserve brand or product names in their original language.\n- All product names MUST be fully translated into the target language, even if they are globally recognized brands or models.\n\n### Length Requirement\n- The summary MUST be <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters INCLUDING spaces.\n- If your draft exceeds the limit, rewrite it shorter until it is within the limit.\n- Preserve key facts; remove less important detail first."
            },
            {
              "id": "1760422024528_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1775644898626",
            "name": "SR_Solution_Summarization Model"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772706317299"
          },
          "code": "SRSOLUTIONSUMMARIZATION_MODEL",
          "id": "1760422133198",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760422133199_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input Data \n- **Title** \n` {{$context.$variables.title}}`\n\n- **ProblemDescription:** \n` {{$context.$variables.problemDescription}}`\n\n- **ResolveDescription:** \n ` {{$context.$variables.resolveDescription}}`\n\n- **Messages (chronological conversation log)**:  \n  Loop through: ` {{$context.$variables.messages}}`\n\nEach message includes:  \n- `MessageContent`  \n- `CreationDate`  \n- `MessageTypeCd` (ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY / ORA_SVC_RESPONSE / ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE)  \n\nUse these inputs to **reconstruct the conversation flow**:  \n- Sort `Messages` in ascending order of `CreationDate`.  \n- Interpret `MessageTypeCd`:  \n  - **ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY** → Customer-reported issue or feedback  \n  - **ORA_SVC_RESPONSE** → Support engineer (SE) responses  \n  - **ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE** → Internal-only notes or system actions (include only if directly relevant)  \n\n---\n\n# Instructions  \nReview the above `Input Data` and produce a summary that focuses only on actions taken by the support engineer and, at the end, the customer’s final action or confirmation. Describe the engineer’s actions and troubleshooting steps in chronological order. Conclude with the customer’s final action/response and the issue status (closed, open, or further action required). Note if any new issues or follow-up requests were created. Keep the summary within {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.  \n\n## SUMMARY LENGTH RULE (MANDATORY)\n\nGenerate the summary so that it number of character count <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.\n\nIf the generated summary exceeds {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}, shorten the wording and regenerate until the summary length is less than or equal to {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}.\n\n---\n\n### Mandatory Guidelines  \n1. **Engineer Actions**  \n   - Present only the support engineer’s actions, troubleshooting steps, fixes, or recommendations in chronological order (no numbering required).  \n\n2. **Customer Final Action**  \n   - After describing the engineer’s actions, add a concise sentence summarizing the customer’s final action/confirmation (e.g., validated fix, provided data, no response).  \n\n3. **Issue Status and New Items**  \n   - State if the issue is closed, remains open, or needs further action, and mention any new issues or follow-ups created.  \n\n4. **Exclusions**  \n   - Do not describe the customer’s original problem or symptoms.  \n   - Exclude greetings, closings, and non-technical chatter.  \n\n5. **Specificity**  \n   - Reference tools, logs, configurations, or artifacts only if used by the engineer.  \n\n6. **Neutral and Concise**  \n   - Use objective, professional language; avoid speculation and opinions.  \n\n7. **Mandatory Fallback -- Insufficient Details**\n- If the combined character count of `Title` + `ProblemDescription` + `ResolveDescription` + `MessageContent` is **<= 100 characters**, first determine whether a meaningful summary can still be generated.\n- If a meaningful summary can be generated, return the summary.\n- If a meaningful summary cannot be generated, return the value of `Title`.\n- Only output exactly:\n  \"Not enough relevant conversational data available to generate a meaningful summary.\"\n  when `Title`, `ProblemDescription`, `ResolveDescription` and all usable `MessageContent` values are missing, empty, null, blank, unreadable, or contain no usable text.\n\n\n---\n\n### Additional Considerations for Accuracy  \n\n**Constraints**  \n- Do not include bullets, headings, recommendations, opinions, or assumptions.  \n- Do not mention message type codes or any system metadata (e.g., ORA_SVC_*).  \n- Use precise, active language and only facts present in the records.  \n\n**Precision**  \n- Distinguish clearly between **customer issue, SE action, and system notes**.  \n- Avoid vague language such as “looked into it” or “worked on it.”  \n\n**No Assumptions**  \n- Do not assume resolution, SR closure, or root cause unless explicitly confirmed.  \n- Do not fabricate details to fill gaps.  \n- Do not infer meaning from redacted placeholders.  \n\n---\n\n### Example Summary  \n\n> The customer reported errors when configuring an Oracle Fusion Application with Oracle Integration Cloud. The support engineer reviewed logs, confirmed events were flowing, and requested customer validation on the OIC side. The customer confirmed the issue persisted and stated that the OIC team found no setup issues. Further troubleshooting or escalation was pending.  \n\n\nSYSTEM RULE – LANGUAGE ENFORCEMENT (HIGHEST PRIORITY):\n\nYou MUST generate the final response strictly in the language specified by:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\nRules:\n- If a valid language code is provided, output MUST be entirely in that language.\n- Do NOT include any words from other languages.\n- If the language code is unsupported or missing, then use the language of the input data.\n- Any violation of this rule makes the response invalid.\n\n---\n\nFINAL OUTPUT VALIDATION (MANDATORY):\n\nBefore returning the final response:\n### Language Validation\n- Perform a strict self-check to ensure EVERY word, phrase, name, and connector is written ONLY in the target language defined by:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n- Do NOT include words, transitional phrases, or grammatical structures in other language.\n- If any other language word or phrase is detected, you MUST translate or replace it before returning the response.\n- Do NOT output the response until it fully passes this language-only validation.\n- Do NOT preserve brand or product names in their original language.\n- All product names MUST be fully translated into the target language, even if they are globally recognized brands or models.\n\n### Length Requirement\n- The summary MUST be <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters INCLUDING spaces.\n- If your draft exceeds the limit, rewrite it shorter until it is within the limit.\n- Preserve key facts; remove less important detail first."
            },
