          },
          "code": "SETUSERMESSAGE",
          "id": "1774015446307",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774015494500",
              "name": "instructions",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{\"User Ask : \" + $context.$system.$inputMessage + \". Interpret and provide only the information that is asked. The response should be to the point and only fulfill requirement that was asked by user. If the provided `Input Data` does not contain enough information to generate the response, only then: `There is no relevant information available to answer the question.`\"}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "setDefaults"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1760420505644"
          },
          "code": "SETDEFAULTS",
          "id": "1774015510660",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774015521879",
              "name": "instructions",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Summarize the Service Request (SR) details from above`Input Data`. This summary should be returned as the response. \nFields to be considered while creating summary are: \n- **SR Attributes** : use only \"Title\", \"ProblemDescription\" fields \n- **Messages** \n\nThe summary should be **clear, factual, and concise paragraph**. The summary must be **professional, third-person, and neutral**, avoiding assumptions. \n\nFocus on the **most important technical issue, key support engineer (SE) actions, and final outcome**.  \nInclude diagnostic steps, intermediate troubleshooting details, and additional follow-ups **only. \n\n### Mandatory Guidelines  \n\n1. **Main Technical Issue**  \n- Explicitly state the **issue reported by the customer**.\n- If the SR was system-generated and the customer did not report any issue, state this clearly.  \n\n2. **Actions Taken by Support Engineer (SE)**  \n- Capture only SE actions, troubleshooting, and clarifications.  \n- Exclude greetings or generic closings.  \n- Mark automation/system-driven responses explicitly as **system-generated actions**.  \n\n3. **Diagnostic Tools/Steps Used**  \n- Mention tools/logs/traces if referenced.  \n- If SE requested data but it was not provided, include this fact.  \n\n4. **Recommendations & Follow-up**  \n- Clearly note SE recommendations, next steps, or escalations.  \n- Do not infer resolution unless the **customer explicitly confirmed it**.  \n\n5. **Customer Interaction Details**  \n- Capture confirmations, additional inputs, or denials.  \n- If no customer updates were provided, include: **\"No customer responses recorded.\"**  \n\n6. **Mandatory Fallback -- Insufficient Details**\n- If the combined character count of `Title` + `ProblemDescription` + `MessageContent` is **<= 100 characters**, first determine whether a meaningful summary can still be generated.\n- If a meaningful summary can be generated, return the summary.\n- If a meaningful summary cannot be generated, return the value of `Title`.\n- Only output exactly:\n  \"Not enough relevant conversational data available to generate a meaningful summary.\"\n  when `Title`, `ProblemDescription`, and all usable `MessageContent` values are missing, empty, null, blank, unreadable, or contain no usable text.\n\n7. **Neutral Terminology**  \n- Always use **support engineer (SE)** and **customer**.  \n- Do not use \"agent,\" personal names, or vague terms.  \n\n\n### Additional Considerations for Accuracy  \n\n**Constraints**  \n- Do not include bullets, headings, recommendations, opinions, or assumptions.  \n- Do not mention message type codes or any system metadata (e.g., ORA_SVC_*).  \n- Use precise, active language and only facts present in the records.  \n\n**Precision**  \n- Distinguish clearly between **customer issue, SE action, and system notes**.  \n- Avoid vague language such as “looked into it” or “worked on it.”  \n\n**No Assumptions**  \n- Do not assume resolution, SR closure, or root cause unless explicitly confirmed.  \n- Do not fabricate details to fill gaps.  \n- Do not infer meaning from redacted placeholders.  \n\n\n### Example Summary  \n\n> The customer reported errors when configuring an Oracle Fusion Application with Oracle Integration Cloud. The support engineer reviewed logs, confirmed events were flowing, and requested customer validation on the OIC side. The customer confirmed the issue persisted and stated that the OIC team found no setup issues. Further troubleshooting or escalation was pending.  \n\n\n### Response Length Rule (MANDATORY)\n\nGenerate the response so that it number of character count <= MAX_RESPONSE_CHAR characters.\nIf the generated response exceeds MAX_RESPONSE_CHAR, shorten the wording and regenerate until the response length is less than or equal to MAX_RESPONSE_CHAR.\n\n\n### Language Enforcement (HIGHEST PRIORITY):\n\nYou MUST generate the final response strictly in the language specified by: LANGUAGE_CD\n\nRules:\n- If a valid language code is provided, output MUST be entirely in that language.\n- Do NOT include any words from other languages.\n- If the language code is unsupported or missing, then use the language of the input data.\n- Any violation of this rule makes the response invalid."
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1775644898626",
            "name": "catchError",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let error = \"\";\n\n  if ($context?.$nodes?.SR_ATTRIBUTES?.$status === \"failure\") {\n    error += \"SR_ATTRIBUTES call failed. \\n\";\n  }\n\n  if ($context?.$nodes?.GET_ALL_SR_MESSAGES?.$status === \"failure\") {\n    error += \"GET_ALL_SR_MESSAGES call failed. \\n\";\n  }\n\n  if ($context?.$nodes?.GET_ALL_MILESTONES?.$status === \"failure\") {\n    error += \"GET_ALL_MILESTONES call failed. \\n\";\n  }\n\n  if ($context?.$nodes?.GET_ALL_ACTIVITIES?.$status === \"failure\") {\n    error += \"GET_ALL_ACTIVITIES call failed. \\n\";\n  }\n\n  if ($context?.$nodes?.GET_PROXY_ATTRIBUTES?.$status === \"failure\") { \n    error += \"GET_ALL_ACTIVITIES call failed. \\n\";\n  }\n\n  if ($context?.$nodes?.GET_PROXY_MESSAGES?.$status === \"failure\") {  \n    error += \"GET_ALL_ACTIVITIES call failed. \\n\";\n  }\n\n  if (error) {\n    throw new Error(error.trim());\n  }\n\n\nreturn \"success\";"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1760414615117"
          },
          "code": "CATCHERROR",
